  "studyDescription": "Researchers conducted a randomized experiment on 90 patients who had suffered a heart attack and were fetched by paramedics. Patients were randomly assigned to receive either a blood thinner (treatment group, n = 40) or a placebo (control group, n = 50) during CPR. The outcome tracked was whether each patient survived to hospital discharge.",
  "variableDescriptions": {
    "group": "Whether the patient was randomly assigned to receive a blood thinner (treatment) or a placebo (control) during CPR.",
    "outcome": "Whether the patient survived to be discharged from the hospital or died."
  },
  "sourceDetail": "OpenIntro IMS, Example 11.1. Based on Böttiger et al. (2001). The blood thinner used was a synthetic version of a naturally occurring enzyme.",
